## Executive Summary

### Purpose of Phase 4

Phase 4 designs the Artha AI backtesting engine — the system that allows trading strategies to be validated against historical Indian market data before being deployed with real capital. It provides a complete simulation environment that reuses the live signal, regime, and risk engines without modification, ensuring that backtest behaviour is structurally identical to live trading behaviour.

The engine covers the full lifecycle: replaying historical candle and tick data, simulating order fills using realistic NSE/NFO execution rules, tracking positions and P&L intrabar, applying transaction costs accurate to Indian market regulations, gating every order through a six-stage risk validation pipeline, and producing post-run analytics and reports that feed the learning engine.

