## Architecture Overview

### High-level architecture

The backtesting engine sits between the Phase 3 database (data source and write target) and the Phase 5 signal/regime/risk engines (logic producers). It acts as a controlled execution environment: it substitutes real-time market data with historical replay, substitutes live broker order routing with a fill simulator, and captures all outputs — trades, executions, positions, equity curve — into the same Phase 3 schema used by live trading.

The fundamental design principle is **engine reuse**: the signal engine, regime engine, and risk engine receive `BarEvent` or `TickEvent` from the replay feed via the same `IMarketDataProvider` interface they use in live mode. They have no awareness of whether time is simulated or real. This guarantees structural parity between backtest and live behaviour.

### Module relationships

```
BacktestRunner (4A)
  │
  ├─ WalkForwardController (4A)     ← fold management, IS/OOS split
  │
  ├─ SimulatedClock (4A)            ← IST bar-step, NSE holiday skip
  │
  ├─ HistoricalDataFeed (4B)        ← implements IMarketDataProvider
  │    ├─ ReplayController (4B)     ← play/pause/resume/seek/speed
  │    ├─ ReplayTickFeed (4B)       ← cursor over ticks table
  │    ├─ ReplayCandleFeed (4B)     ← windowed read from candles
  │    └─ EventMerger (4B)         ← merges tick+candle by exchange_ts
  │
  ├─ [SignalEngine] (Phase 5)       ← consumes BarEvent via ReplayEventBus
  ├─ [RegimeEngine] (Phase 5)       ← consumes BarEvent, classifies regime
  │
  ├─ RiskValidationPipeline (4E)    ← 6 stages, gates every order
  │
  ├─ TradeSimulationEngine (4C)
  │    ├─ EntrySimulator (4C)       ← MARKET/LIMIT/SL-M fill model
  │    ├─ ExitSimulator (4C)        ← full/partial/forced exit
  │    ├─ SLManager (4C)            ← fixed/trailing/time-based SL
  │    ├─ TargetManager (4C)        ← fixed/scaled/R-multiple TP
  │    └─ PositionTracker (4C)      ← in-memory MTM, MAE/MFE per bar
  │
  ├─ CostAggregator (4D)
  │    ├─ BrokerageModel (4D)       ← zero/flat-fee/percentage profiles
  │    ├─ SlippageModel (4D)        ← zero/fixed/pct/spread/volume-adj
  │    └─ TransactionCostModel (4D) ← STT/CTT, exchange, SEBI, stamp, GST
  │
  ├─ AnalyticsEngine (4F)           ← post-run, 7 metrics
  │
  └─ ReportOrchestrator (4G)        ← 5 parallel report builders
```

### Event flow

One complete bar step through the full engine:

```
SimulatedClock advances one IST bar
  → HistoricalDataFeed emits BarEvent (+ TickEvents if mixed mode)
  → EventMerger orders by exchange_ts
  → ReplayEventBus delivers to RegimeEngine
  → RegimeEngine classifies regime label
  → ReplayEventBus delivers to SignalEngine
  → SignalEngine evaluates indicators → emits SignalEvent (or null)
  → RiskValidationPipeline: 6 stages → approved_qty or rejection
  → EntrySimulator: fill price + CostAggregator
  → PositionTracker: MTM update, MAE/MFE tracking
  → SLManager + TargetManager: check breach on every tick/bar
  → ExitSimulator (on breach): fill + CostAggregator
  → DB writes: trades, executions, positions, equity_curve
  → On trade close: learning_records written

After strategy_runs.status = completed:
  → AnalyticsEngine: 7 metrics → performance_metrics upsert
  → ReportOrchestrator: 5 builders in parallel → ReportRegistry
```

