## Phase 4E — Risk Validation Pipeline

### Objectives

Design the six-stage risk validation pipeline that gates every signal before it becomes an order. Enforce position sizing, daily loss limits, portfolio drawdown floors, exposure concentration, concurrent position limits, and margin availability — all in-memory, synchronously, on the hot path.

### Design decisions

**Pipeline, not a single gate.** Six independent stages run in sequence. Each stage can independently reject or (Stage 1 only) resize the order. Pipeline halts at first rejection — remaining stages skipped.

**All checks are pure in-memory comparisons.** `RiskState` is maintained by `RiskEngine` across the bar loop. No DB reads during validation. `RiskState` is updated by `PositionTracker` after each fill and each bar close.

**Rejected signals are training data.** `signal.status = rejected` and `RiskValidationResult` stored on the signal row (`signals.features` JSONB gets a `risk_rejection` key). The learning engine trains on rejected signals as well as acted signals.

**Daily loss circuit breaker is session-scoped and irrecoverable.** Once `daily_loss_limit_breached = true` on `RiskState`, no new entries for the rest of the trading session — even if open positions recover MTM. Resets at 09:15 IST next session.

**Unrealised loss included in daily loss calculation.** `session_total_loss = session_realised_pnl + session_unrealised_pnl`. A strategy with ₹40K realised loss and ₹15K open unrealised loss has consumed ₹55K of risk budget. More conservative than NSE RMS definition; correct for simulation accuracy.

**Max drawdown check is fold-level.** `portfolio_peak_value` is the high-water mark across the entire fold. Once breached, the fold is marked `drawdown_halted` and `WalkForwardController` is notified. No recovery within fold.

**Kelly → qty sizing in Stage 1.** Five steps: Kelly fraction to raw notional → notional cap → raw qty from notional → lot-size alignment → min-notional floor check. Resize (not reject) at notional cap; reject if `qty < lot_size` after alignment.

**Opposing direction block is separate from same-symbol block.** Cannot open SHORT while LONG is open in same symbol even when `allow_pyramid = true`. Reversals require explicit close first.

**Margin requirements are SPAN-approximated.** `span_margin_rate` loaded from `CostConfig` — not fetched from NSE live SPAN calculator. Conservative flat rates: 12% NIFTY futures, 15% stock futures, 35% short options. Long options margin = premium only (max loss).

### Outputs

`RiskValidationResult` shape: `{ passed: boolean, stage: 1–6, reason: string | null, adjusted_qty: number | null, detail: string }`.

Six validation stages:

| Stage | Name | Reject or Resize |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Position sizing | Resize at notional cap; reject below min lot |
| 2 | Daily loss limit | Reject; circuit breaker irrecoverable within session |
| 3 | Max drawdown floor | Reject; fold-level circuit breaker |
| 4 | Exposure limits | Reject (symbol / segment / gross / net sub-checks) |
| 5 | Concurrent positions | Reject (max open trades / same-symbol / opposing direction) |
| 6 | Margin availability | Reject; margin reserved on approval |

`RiskState` fields: `session_realised_pnl`, `session_unrealised_pnl`, `portfolio_peak_value`, `portfolio_current_value`, `gross_exposure`, `net_exposure`, `exposure_by_symbol`, `exposure_by_segment`, `open_trade_count`, `open_symbols`, `cash_available`, `margin_used`, `daily_limit_hit`.

